# Shared Plug-in Contract v0.3 — runtime, package manifest and host; repo placement decided by HoP, path set at publication [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]

> One host-neutral plug-in contract, living in ComposeIO's public repo, that both ComposeIO and Gnomon implement. A plug-in is declared at three layers: R (runtime, spec 85 `ComposePlugin`, unchanged), P (a static `manifest.json` a host reads and renders for consent BEFORE any plug-in code is imported), H (the host: it owns consent, owns its own manifest section, and mounts a shared plain-web Plugin Manager). The contract is authoritative: when two hosts disagree, the host whose behaviour differs has the bug, and the arbiter is a hello-world conformance script both hosts run against their pinned contract version. v0.1 is exactly the size hello-world exercises. (0.3) Contract 0.3 is an additive MINOR that freezes the manifest schema, adds optional `capabilities` and `warnings`, asks consent only at grant changes, makes a refuse always stop, and records every state-changing operation with its operator; section 18 is the delta and section 19 holds its open decisions.

---

