## 11. The host sections

### [CXC-PC-HOST-SECTIONS] `hosts`: presence means supported; each host owns its own section's schema and ignores the others'

- rule: (1) `hosts` MUST have at least one key. (2) A key's PRESENCE means that host is supported. (3) Each host owns the schema of its OWN section and MUST ignore every other host's section. (4) A host's section permissions MUST appear on the consent screen through THAT host's renderer ([CXC-PC-CONSENT-CONTENT]). (5) The contract defines only these rules; Gnomon's section contents are specified in Gnomon spec 50, revised, and are only RESERVED here. Pointer: Gnomon spec 50 ((a local path, not published), node GM-PLG-R-SECTION) defines the gnomon: section. A host that implements v0.1 never auto-upgrades ([CXC-PC-LIFECYCLE-UPGRADE]). (6) ComposeIO's section in v0.1 is empty or `{}`: its presence declares support and it holds nothing yet.
- default: the `composeio` section is `{}`.
- unknown-host-keys: keys in `hosts` naming hosts this host does not know are IGNORED (other hosts may exist); they are not refused as unknown core keys.
- own-key-absent: if the installing host's OWN key is absent, the install is REFUSED with the message "not supported on host <name>".
- boundary-case: a plug-in whose `hosts` lacks the key of the host being installed on is REFUSED with "not supported on host <name>".
- verify-machine: hello-world (both keys) installs on both hosts; a manifest with only `gnomon` is refused on ComposeIO with exactly "not supported on host composeio"; a manifest with `composeio`, `gnomon` and an extra `otherhost` key installs and `otherhost` is ignored; ComposeIO ignores arbitrary content in `hosts.gnomon`.
- verify-human: none required.
- status: proposed
- status-detail: proposed — awaiting ratify
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the section list is gnomon-architect's statement of its needs; the contract-side rules are the architect's; full provenance in the r23 revision record
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-UNKNOWN-KEYS], [CXC-PC-CONSENT-CONTENT], [CXC-PC-PRE-INTEGRATION]
- host-name-rule: A host name, which is a key of `hosts` and the prefix of its host-section grants, matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$` and is never `bus`, `code` or `permission`, the prefixes of the built-in grant forms. So no host's grants can collide with `bus.publish:`, `bus.subscribe:`, `code:`, `permission.network:` or `permission.filesystem:`. A manifest whose `hosts` holds a name breaking this rule is refused, naming it. The host's own name is checked against the same rule when the library is constructed. (`permission` added in r21 with the permission grant forms, composeux-architect 2026-11-26, architect-synthesis.)

