## 12. Version rule

### [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE] `contract: "MAJOR.MINOR"`; a newer plug-in is REFUSED by an older host with both versions named — the NEW plug-in breaks first

- rule: (1) `contract` is `"MAJOR.MINOR"`. (2) A MINOR bump is ADDITIVE (new optional fields, or reserved names adopted). (3) A MAJOR bump is any change to the MEANING of an existing field. (4) A host implements ONE contract version. It accepts a manifest with the same MAJOR and a MINOR at or below its own. (5) A manifest written against a newer MINOR, or a different MAJOR, is REFUSED at install, with BOTH versions named.
- which-side-breaks-first: the NEW plug-in fails loudly on the OLD host; the host never half-reads a manifest it does not fully understand. The old host and its installed plug-ins keep working.
- default: none; `contract` is required.
- boundary-case: a missing, non-string or malformed `contract` is refused naming the value.
- verify-machine: [CXC-PC-NC-CONTRACT-MISMATCH] (`"0.3"` on a 0.2 host); and positive controls: `"0.2"` on a 0.2 host installs; `"0.1"` on a 0.2 host installs (same MAJOR, lower MINOR).
- verify-human: the refusal text on the glass names both versions.
- status: proposed
- status-detail: proposed — awaiting ratify
- provenance: architect-synthesis — Plumb's addendum to the brief.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-CONTRACT-AUTHORITATIVE], [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS], [CXC-PC-NC-CONTRACT-MISMATCH]
- v0-3-delta: (0.3) The host's version is "0.3" and rules (1) to (5) are unchanged. The version the library accepts is stated at CXC-PC-V03-VERSION-0-3; the freeze that follows from rules (2) and (3) is stated at CXC-PC-V03-MANIFEST-FROZEN.

### [CXC-PC-CONTRACT-AUTHORITATIVE] When the two hosts disagree, the contract is authoritative and the host whose behaviour differs has the bug

- rule: the contract spec is AUTHORITATIVE. When ComposeIO and Gnomon disagree, the host whose behaviour differs from the contract is the one with the bug. The ARBITER is the conformance suite: the hello-world lifecycle script ships with the library, and BOTH hosts run it against their pinned contract version.
- verify-machine: a host that fails any step of [CXC-PC-CONFORMANCE-SCRIPT] or any negative control is non-conformant by definition, regardless of which host is older.
- verify-human: none required.
- status: proposed
- status-detail: proposed — awaiting ratify
- provenance: architect-synthesis — Plumb's addendum.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-CONFORMANCE-SCRIPT]

### [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS] The contract changes only by a new tagged release `plugin-contract-vX.Y`, cut with the library

- rule: the contract MUST change only by a new tagged release named `plugin-contract-vX.Y`, cut with the library. Gnomon and ComposeIO each move by BUMPING their pin. A contract edit is NEVER a silent edit.
- verify-machine: the contract JSON Schema and this spec carry the same `contract` version string as the git tag at release; a CI check fails when the schema changes without a version bump.
- verify-human: none required.
- status: proposed
- status-detail: proposed — awaiting ratify
- provenance: architect-synthesis — Plumb's addendum.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-LIBRARY]

### [CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION] Standing rule: a host-side change cites the contract version it implements

- rule: "a host-side change cites the contract version it implements." This is a standing order for BOTH checklists: GM-SPEC-CHECKLIST (Gnomon) and ComposeIO's spec checklist each gain it. Where ComposeIO's checklist lives: `checklist-home`.
- checklist-home: ComposeIO's spec checklist EXISTS as 96-composeio-spec-checklist.lts ([SPEC:CXC-SPEC-CHECKLIST]), with CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION as its first rule; it IS registered in PROC-SPEC-AUDIT (key product-checklists-addendum-2026-11-26, verified by Plumb 2026-11-26T02:16:06Z) (AUDIT_DELTA_r13 E9, r14).
- checklist-candidates: candidate rules for ComposeIO's spec checklist (the audit's extension points) are listed at [CXC-PC-PRE-INTEGRATION].
- verify-machine: the ComposeIO spec checklist file exists and its first rule is this one (evidence slot at [CXC-PC-EVIDENCE], `evidence-composeio-checklist`); GM-SPEC-CHECKLIST carries the rule.
- verify-human: none required.
- status: proposed
- status-detail: proposed — awaiting ratify
- provenance: architect-synthesis — Plumb's addendum. `checklist-home` recorded at r12 (audit CONFORMANCE).
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS]

