- see-also: [CXC-PC-RULE-SIZE], [CXC-CS-DEFAULT-PLUGINS]

### [CXC-PC-PROVING-ORDER] HoP's proving order: hello-world, then print-services, then the bus-participant extension — which needs more than v0.1's own-namespace rule

- consequence: that extension reads and publishes on namespaces other than its own, which v0.1's rule (every bus namespace MUST sit under `plugins/<domain>/`, [CXC-PC-BUS-BLOCK]) cannot express. v0.1 keeps the own-namespace rule; the selector-scoped `bus.read` / `bus.publish` permission form is RESERVED for v0.2 ([CXC-PC-RESERVED-NAMES]).
- verify-machine: none — a recorded ordering and a recorded consequence; the schema carries no `bus.read` / `bus.publish` form.
- verify-human: none required.
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — HoP's ordering (his comment); the reservation is the architect's ruling 2026-11-26 (audit M2)
- provenance: david-ruling for the ordering (HoP's adopted comment, wording drafted by gnomon-architect) and his D1 selection; architect-synthesis for the consequence and the reservation.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-RESERVED-NAMES], [CXC-PC-BUS-BLOCK], [CXC-PC-HELLO-V1]

### v0.2 notes: the reviewer's 14 areas and 4 hardening checks are not extended in v0.2 without HoP's word; v0.1 keeps every one exactly as built [CXC-PC-V0-2-GROWTH-GUARD]

- v0-2-guard: v0.2 work MUST NOT extend any area listed in this node's area and hardening keys without HoP's word. v0.1's CODE keeps all 14 areas and all 4 checks exactly as built (compose-plugins as QA-passed). In v0.1's SPEC TEXT, areas 1 to 12 and the 4 checks stay unchanged; areas 13 and 14 are spec text moved out of spec 95 in r23 under D2 (to the revision record, and to a pointer to Gnomon spec 50). This node changes no v0.1 rule.
- area-01: the spelling rules for network targets and file paths in permissions (host-name grammar, canonical IPv4, RFC 5952 IPv6, port range, IDN and zone-id refusals, POSIX path grammar, 4096-byte cap) [CXC-PC-PERMISSIONS]
- area-02: the duplicate-entry refusal and the two commentary notes in permissions (duplicates, never-verified-scope, host-duties-unchanged) [CXC-PC-PERMISSIONS]
- area-03: the rule that read-write covers read in upgrades (permissions-widen) [CXC-PC-CONSENT-WIDENING]
- area-04: the list of about 35 reserved Home Assistant names (ha-reserved-keys, ha-other-names-reserved) [CXC-PC-RESERVED-NAMES]
- area-05: the clause that lowering isolation_floor forces fresh consent (granted-format, widening-definition, raised-floor) [CXC-PC-CONSENT-RECORD]
- area-06: the automatic move of a colliding in-process plug-in to a subprocess (inprocess-collision, inprocess-collision-details) [CXC-PC-HOST-ISOLATION-CHOICE]
- area-07: the code: consent entry and its widening rule (code-is-a-permission) [CXC-PC-CONSENT-WIDENING]
- area-08: the exact-pin grammar and PEP 503 name normalization for requirements (validator-readings (5), host-provided-packages) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- area-09: the optional manifest fields codeowners and issue_tracker [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- area-10: the cross-runtime regex agreement test for the shipped JSON Schema (validator-readings (15)) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- area-11: the mutation check on every negative control (verify-machine) [CXC-PC-NEGATIVE-CONTROLS]
- area-12: ComposeIO's HTTP Basic-auth login detail for the Plugin Manager (composeio-auth-hook at [CXC-PC-COMPOSEIO-HOST-IDENTITY]; kept in spec 95 until a ComposeIO host spec exists, per the r23 delta audit F1; the code stays in the ComposeIO host)
- area-13: the three nodes that only recorded rejected options: the manifest-format choice, no entry-point discovery, no pluggy (moved out of spec 95 in r23 under D2)
- area-14: the restated list of Gnomon's host-section contents (replaced by a pointer to Gnomon spec 50 in r23 under D2) [CXC-PC-HOST-SECTIONS]
- hardening-01: the refusal of a symlinked manifest.json or of a standard_questions path through a symlink leaving the package (validator-readings (7), QA N5) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- hardening-02: the refusal of NaN, Infinity and out-of-range numbers such as 1e999 in the manifest (validator-readings (8), QA G1) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- hardening-03: the Unicode format-character and U+2028/U+2029 line-separator rules, frozen at Unicode 15.1, also on consent-record text (validator-readings (12), QA N3, E2, E4) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- hardening-04: the 256 KiB size and 64-level nesting limits on manifest.json (validator-readings (14), QA N1) [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS]
- list-source: the independent Sonnet reviewer's core-cut proposal for r22, sections 2 and 4 ((a private draft, in the private companion)): its D1 items (1) to (14) and its D3 four known-limit candidates
- status: decided
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-RULE-SIZE], [CXC-PC-RESERVED-NAMES], [CXC-PC-PROVING-ORDER]

