### [CXC-PC-ARCHITECT-PROPOSALS] Every node with provenance architect-synthesis is a proposal — list them by QUERY, not from a hand list

- how-to-list: every node of this spec whose `provenance` LEADS WITH `architect-synthesis` is a proposal awaiting ratify. List them with `lts_find(corpus="intelligence-console", source_file="95-plugin-contract.lts", all_of=["architect-synthesis"], none_of=["david-ruling", "david-selection"], fields=["provenance"])`. The `none_of` excludes every node whose provenance leads with `david-ruling` or `david-selection` (HoP's ruling or his DSD selection): those nodes are decided, and they are treated alike. Measured at r14: no provenance that leads with `architect-synthesis` mentions either class, so this substring exclusion equals "leads with". A node excluded this way may still carry an `architect-synthesis` half (it says which half is which); list those mixed nodes with `all_of=["architect-synthesis"], any_of=["david-ruling", "david-selection"], fields=["provenance"]`. Do NOT use `where provenance equals`: many values carry a trailing explanation, so exact equality misses them. A spec that adds a provenance class updates this query (AUDIT_DELTA_r13 X1, r14).
- why: the first draft kept a hand list of ten proposals while 48 nodes were proposals; the 2026-11-26 audit measured the index as incomplete. No hand list is kept.
- note: the narrative marks the proposals as the architect's; none is a recorded HoP or David ruling unless its `provenance` says so.
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided-by-architect — replaced by a query pointer at the audit revision, 2026-11-26
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [DX-INTERPRETATION-IS-AN-INFERENCE], [CXC-PC-PRE-INTEGRATION]

