### A host that offers consent for a manifest declaring `eula` MUST show the EULA text in full, or refuse the install [CXC-PC-V02-EULA-HOST-OBLIGATION]

- rule: (1) a host whose consent screen offers accept for a prompt whose `content.eula` is not None MUST show `content.eula.text` exactly and in full on that screen, before the accept control. (2) A host that cannot show it MUST refuse to install that manifest, naming `eula` or the digest argument `consented_eula_sha256`, and MUST NOT offer accept without it. (3) The library's own web manager does so (CXC-PC-V02-EULA-DISPLAY item 3). (4) The `eula_sha256` in a consent record is therefore always the digest of text the operator was offered.
- exactly-and-in-full: the text appears as a contiguous, unaltered string; scrolling or paging that reaches all of it counts; a summary, a truncation, a newline normalisation or a different rendering of the same words does not.
- composeio-cli: ComposeIO's CLI install path passes no EULA digest, so it refuses a manifest that declares `eula` with `EulaShaMismatch`, whose message names `consented_eula_sha256` rather than `eula`; that is the refusal of item (2) and is accepted as meeting it. A CLI that wants to install such a manifest must print `ConsentContent.text()` (which carries the EULA block) and pass the digest back.
- conformance-helper: the library ships a fixture package `hello-world-eula` (a hello-world v1 manifest with `contract` "0.2" and an `eula` naming a text file of at least three lines containing a tab and a non-ASCII character) and a function `eula_text_shown(rendered: str, prompt) -> bool`. It returns True only if `prompt.content.eula.text` occurs in `rendered` as a contiguous substring, after HTML unescaping when `rendered` is HTML. Each host's own consent-screen test renders its screen for a prompt of that fixture and asserts the helper returns True; a host with no screen asserts that install of the fixture is refused naming `eula`. The helper is not a step of the 9-step script and not a negative control, so guard area-11 is not extended. The helper treats `rendered` as HTML, and unescapes it before the search, only when it begins with `<!doctype html` or `<html`; any other string is searched as given, so a text-only screen is compared without unescaping.
- default: a manifest without `eula` is unaffected.
- boundary-case: a screen that shows the first 1000 characters and a link, a screen that shows a summary, and a screen that converts line feeds to spaces each make the helper return False.
- verify-machine: the library's web consent screen for the fixture makes the helper True; a rendering with the text truncated, one with line feeds converted to spaces, and one with a different text of the same length each make it False; each host's own test (Gnomon's consent screen test, ComposeIO's web manager) asserts True for its screen.
- verify-human: an operator on each host reads the fixture's EULA in full on that host's consent screen before accepting.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-EULA-HOST-OBLIGATION]
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_license_eula.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_EULA_HOST_OBLIGATION; python/tests/test_composeserver_plugins.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_EULA_HOST_OBLIGATION_composeio_web_manager; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name); the ComposeIO host suites at that commit: 45 passed, rc 0 (raw output sha256 15732a62348e64b59a09dc99a8ea554f93a0675775bcd0187c9458a9d2054dba); independent candidate review at that commit, round 2: PASS_WITH_NOTES. Filled 2026-11-27 from the build, review and push reports.
