### `PluginManager.record_decline(prompt, *, decided_by)` appends exactly one refusal record for the prepared prompt the operator saw, and returns it [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE]

- signature: `record_decline(self, prompt: ConsentPrompt, *, decided_by: str) -> ConsentRecord`; `decided_by` is keyword-only and has no default.
- accepts: a `ConsentPrompt` returned by THIS manager's `prepare_install` (kind "install") or `prepare_upgrade` (kind "upgrade"). There is no uninstall prompt (see CXC-PC-V02-RULING-UNINSTALL-RECORD).
- writes: exactly ONE line to the consent store, through the same `ConsentStore.append` that the private `_gate` uses and built by the same record constructor: `domain`, `version` and `manifest_sha256` from the prompt; `granted` equal to the prompt's `content.granted` (what the operator was offered); `decided_by` from the argument; `decided_at` from the clock; `host` the manager's host name; `decision: "refused"`; and `eula_sha256` when the prompt carries a EULA (CXC-PC-V02-EULA-HASH-RECORD).
- returns: the record that was appended.
- validation: `decided_by` obeys the consent-record text rules already enforced by the record constructor (non-empty, one line); a violation raises the constructor's `ConsentRefused` naming `decided_by`, and because the record is constructed before the append, nothing is written.
- refusals: a prompt that is not one this manager prepared raises `PromptNotPrepared`; a stale one raises `PromptStale` (CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE-PROMPT-VALIDITY). Both are subclasses of `PluginContractRefusal` and both are exported from `compose_plugins`.
- unchanged: the gate's own refusal path (`install` or `upgrade` with a refusing decision) still writes its refusal record exactly as in 0.1; `record_decline` adds a way to write one without calling those operations, nothing more.
- default: none; the caller supplies the prompt and `decided_by`.
- boundary-case: `decided_by=""`, a `decided_by` containing U+2028, and a non-string `decided_by` are each refused naming `decided_by`, with the consent store unchanged.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-ONE-RECORD-NOTHING-ELSE-CHANGES (one record, the record's eight fields, the returned value equal to the line written) and CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-INSTALLED-DOMAIN-UNCHANGED; the boundary table above through the same test harness.
- verify-human: none required — fully machine-observable.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-ONE-RECORD-NOTHING-ELSE-CHANGES], [CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-INSTALLED-DOMAIN-UNCHANGED]
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_record_decline.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_RD_ONE_RECORD_NOTHING_ELSE_CHANGES, test_CXC_PC_V02_T_RD_ONE_RECORD_NOTHING_ELSE_CHANGES_decided_by_refused, test_CXC_PC_V02_T_RD_INSTALLED_DOMAIN_UNCHANGED; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name); independent candidate review at that commit, round 2: PASS_WITH_NOTES. Filled 2026-11-27 from the build, review and push reports.
- evidence-fills-with: raw output of the six record_decline contract tests, the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- decision-source: DEC-PLUGIN-RECORD-DECLINE-CALL-V0-2-2026-11-27; Plumb's touchpoint answer plumb-work:PLB-DEC-COMPOSE-PLUGINS-V0-2-RECORD-DECLINE-TOUCHPOINT-2026-11-27 (GO on design, six contract tests)
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — ratified by DEC-SPEC95-V0-2-DELTA-RATIFIED-2026-11-27 (decided and cleared by Plumb on design; the record keeps its eight keys, CXC-PC-V02-RULING-RECORD-KIND)
- provenance: architect-synthesis — decided by the contract owner; shape expanded by the writer from the owner's decision and gnomon-architect's delta
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
