- see-also: [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE], [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE-SIDE-EFFECTS]

### Test 2: a decline on an installed domain leaves its record, version, state, running plug-in and config unchanged [CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-INSTALLED-DOMAIN-UNCHANGED]

- procedure: install v1, enable it and let it reach running, once; then repeat with the plug-in installed and stopped (state `installed`). The second repeat cannot use `disabled`: `prepare_upgrade` is refused from `disabled` (CXC-PC-LIFECYCLE-STATES allows upgrade only from `installed` or `enabled`), and a prompt prepared while enabled is stale once the plug-in is disabled. In each case take Q from `prepare_upgrade`; deep-copy the install record; note the identity of `M.running(domain)` (None when stopped), the counter `M.instantiations`, the stored config and a hash of the installed code tree; call `record_decline`.
- asserts: the install record deep-equals the copy; `M.state(domain)` and `M.status(domain)` are as before; the running object is the same object; `instantiations` is unchanged; the config and the code-tree hash are unchanged; the bus spy recorded no publish.
- verify-machine: non-zero exit on any difference.
- verify-human: none required.
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_record_decline.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_RD_INSTALLED_DOMAIN_UNCHANGED; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name). Filled 2026-11-27 from the build and push reports.
- status: decided
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE], [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE-SIDE-EFFECTS]

### Test 3: a concurrent record_decline and upgrade never produce an upgrade from the decline [CXC-PC-V02-T-RD-CONCURRENT-WITH-UPGRADE]

- procedure: 200 iterations, each on a fresh state root with v1 installed. Two threads start together from a barrier, in random order. Variant A: thread 1 calls `record_decline(Q, decided_by="op-a")` and thread 2 calls `upgrade` on Q's package with the host gate refusing. Variant B: thread 2 calls `upgrade` with the host gate granting. After each iteration read the install record, installs.json and consent.jsonl.
- asserts: in Variant A the installed version is v1 in EVERY iteration and no `granted` record exists. In Variant B the final state is v2 only if the upgrade's own gate granted it; and in no iteration does a `refused` record with decided_by "op-a" follow a `granted` record for the same manifest_sha256 (a decline is never written after the upgrade consumed its prompt); a decline that lost the race raised `PromptStale` and wrote nothing. In every iteration installs.json parses and consent.jsonl parses line by line.
- verify-machine: non-zero exit on any violated assertion in any iteration.
- verify-human: none required.
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_record_decline.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_RD_CONCURRENT_WITH_UPGRADE; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name). Filled 2026-11-27 from the build and push reports.
- status: decided
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE-PROMPT-VALIDITY], [CXC-PC-V02-RECORD-DECLINE-SIDE-EFFECTS]

