### The manager reports a log event that its snapshot does not reflect, and a snapshot that is ahead of its log, and it neither repairs nor blocks [CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-DIVERGENCE]

- rule: `PluginManager.install_log_findings()` (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-FINDINGS-METHOD) compares the VALID events of the log with `installs.json`. For each domain take the highest-`seq` valid event that is not an `abort` and is not named by a later `abort`'s `aborts_seq`: finding kind `unreflected-event` when the domain's record has an `event_seq` lower than that event's `seq`, or no record at all. Finding kind `snapshot-ahead` for a record whose `event_seq` exceeds the highest valid `seq` of the log ("the log is behind the snapshot").
- finding-text: the `message` of `unreflected-event` is `installs.jsonl event <seq> (<event> of <domain> <version>) is not reflected in installs.json (record is at event <n>)`; of `snapshot-ahead` it is `installs.json record for <domain> is at event <n>, beyond the last event <last> of installs.jsonl`.
- shown: the web manager's index page lists the `message` of every finding, from `install_log_findings()` and no other source, under a heading "Install log findings" when there is at least one, and shows nothing, byte for byte as in 0.1, when there is none.
- no-repair-no-block: the manager does not append, edit or delete anything in response to a finding and does not refuse any operation because of one (ruled: CXC-PC-V02-RULING-INSTALL-LOG-FAILURE-POLICY). A repair is a person's decision.
- scope: a state root written by a 0.1 library (records without `event_seq`, no log) yields no finding.
- known-limit: the check sees only the highest un-aborted event per domain; an earlier un-aborted dangling event that a later successful event followed is not reported, because the later event's snapshot proves the domain moved on.
- default: `install_log_findings()` returns `()` when there is nothing to report.
- boundary-case: an empty log with records that carry `event_seq` is a "log is behind" finding for each such record.
- verify-machine: a state root with event N in the log and the record at N-1 yields exactly one finding naming N; the record at N yields none; an event followed by its abort yields none; a record whose `event_seq` exceeds the last event yields the "behind" finding; a 0.1 state root yields none; the index page for a state root with a finding contains the heading and the finding text, and for one without is byte-identical to the 0.1 index page except for the footer's contract version; a finding does not stop an `enable` from succeeding; each finding is returned as an `InstallLogFinding` with kind `unreflected-event` or `snapshot-ahead`.
- verify-human: an operator who had the host killed during an upgrade sees the finding on the manager's front page and can tell which transition did not complete.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-INSTALL-LOG-DIVERGENCE]
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_install_log.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_INSTALL_LOG_DIVERGENCE; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name); independent candidate review at that commit, round 2: PASS_WITH_NOTES. Filled 2026-11-27 from the build, review and push reports.
- evidence-fills-with: raw test output, the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- decision-source: follows from the write-ahead ordering of the requester's ask; the report-only policy is ruled at CXC-PC-V02-RULING-INSTALL-LOG-FAILURE-POLICY
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — ratified by DEC-SPEC95-V0-2-DELTA-RATIFIED-2026-11-27 (see CXC-PC-V02-RULING-INSTALL-LOG-FAILURE-POLICY)
