### The install-log findings are exposed by a manager method that returns structured findings, not only on the web index [CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-FINDINGS-METHOD]

- rule: (1) `PluginManager.install_log_findings(self) -> tuple[InstallLogFinding, ...]` is a METHOD. It replaces the attribute and the `check_install_log()` call that an earlier draft of this delta named; neither was ever shipped. (2) Each call reads `installs.jsonl` and `installs.json` afresh, caches nothing, writes nothing, and never raises: a failure to read EITHER file becomes an `unreadable` finding that carries the exception class name only (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-FAILURE-TEXT). (3) `InstallLogFinding` is a frozen dataclass exported from `compose_plugins` with the fields `kind: str`, `domain: str | None`, `seq: int | None`, `line: int | None`, `code: str | None`, `message: str`. (4) `kind` is one of `unreflected-event`, `snapshot-ahead` (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-DIVERGENCE), `malformed-line`, `seq-gap`, `unreadable` (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-MALFORMED-LINES); `code` is set for `malformed-line` (its reason code) and is None otherwise; `domain` is None for kinds that name no domain; `line` is set for `malformed-line` and `seq-gap`; `seq` is set for `unreflected-event` and `seq-gap`. (5) The tuple is sorted by (kind, domain or the empty string, line or 0, seq or 0) so two calls on the same files return equal tuples. (6) `()` means nothing to report. (7) The web index renders the `message` of each finding from this method and from no other source. (8) The messages are: `malformed-line`: `installs.jsonl line <line> is malformed (<code>) and is skipped`; `seq-gap`: `installs.jsonl seq jumps to <seq> at line <line>`; `unreadable`: `installs.jsonl cannot be read (<ClassName>)` for the log and `installs.json cannot be read (<ClassName>)` for the snapshot (an unreadable snapshot is reported, and the divergence kinds are then not computed); the other two as at CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-DIVERGENCE.
- why: a host decides what to do about a finding (Gnomon raises an alert); it cannot do so from HTML.
- default: no log and no records: `()`.
- boundary-case: a manager constructed on a log with problems and the method called twice returns the same tuple; a finding resolved by a later successful event no longer appears on the next call.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V02-T-INSTALL-LOG-FINDINGS-METHOD: a state root with an unreflected event, a snapshot ahead, a garbage line, a gap and an unreadable log and an unreadable `installs.json` (one scenario each) returns, for each, exactly one finding of the right `kind` with the fields set as in (4); `isinstance(result, tuple)` and each item is an `InstallLogFinding`; two calls return equal tuples; the method writes nothing (the state root is byte-identical, mtimes included); the web index shows the same `message` strings; a clean state returns `()`; the dataclass is frozen (assignment raises).
- verify-human: an operator sees on the manager's front page the same findings a host's alert shows.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-INSTALL-LOG-FINDINGS-METHOD]
