### The 0.1 schema file stays byte-identical and a new 0.2 schema file is selected by the manifest's `contract` [CXC-PC-V02-SCHEMA-FILES]

- rule: (1) `manifest-0.1.schema.json` is byte-identical to the file shipped with compose-plugins 0.1.0, still reports `x-compose-plugins-contract: "0.1"` and has no `license` or `eula`. (2) `manifest-0.2.schema.json` is new: it reports `x-compose-plugins-contract: "0.2"` and carries every 0.1 field plus `license` and `eula` (CXC-PC-V02-LICENSE-FIELD, CXC-PC-V02-EULA-FIELD). (3) The schema that validates a manifest is chosen by that manifest's `contract` value: "0.1" selects the 0.1 file, "0.2" the 0.2 file; any other value is refused by the version rule before a schema is chosen. (4) A manifest that states "0.1" and carries `license` or `eula` is therefore refused by the 0.1 schema as well as by the validator rule (CXC-PC-V02-VERSION-0-2 rule (3)). (5) The existing agreement test between each schema file and the validator runs on the 0.2 file as on any shipped schema; this node adds no case to the adversarial set of `validator-readings` (15).
- why: readers and tools pinned to the 0.1 schema keep working unchanged; the version is carried by the file, not by an edit of an old file.
- default: none.
- boundary-case: a 0.2 manifest carrying neither new field validates against both files' field set but is selected the 0.2 file; a manifest whose `contract` is missing or malformed is refused before selection, as CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE says.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V02-T-SCHEMA-FILES: the sha256 of `manifest-0.1.schema.json` equals that of the file inside the published 0.1.0 wheel; the 0.1 file contains neither `license` nor `eula`; the 0.2 file reports "0.2" and contains both; a 0.1 manifest with `eula` fails the 0.1 schema and the validator; the same manifest at "0.2" passes the 0.2 schema; the file chosen for each of the eight rows of CXC-PC-V02-T-VERSION-GATES-THE-NEW-KEYS is as rule (3) says.
- verify-human: none required — structural.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-SCHEMA-FILES]
