### The library's web manager never uninstalls on one click: it shows what will be removed and waits for a second, explicit confirm [CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM]

- rule: (1) the plug-in detail page's uninstall button posts to `<prefix>/plugin/<domain>/uninstall/prepare`. (2) `POST .../uninstall/prepare` (behind the host's auth hook and the CSRF defence, like every POST) changes nothing and renders the confirm screen. (3) `POST .../uninstall/decide` (same hook and defence) with `decision=confirm` calls `PluginManager.uninstall(domain)` after the stale check (CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM-BINDING) and redirects to the index page; any other `decision` value, including `cancel` and a missing one, changes nothing, writes nothing and redirects to the plug-in's detail page. (4) The 0.1 route `POST .../uninstall` no longer uninstalls: it behaves exactly as `.../uninstall/prepare`. (5) `PluginManager.uninstall` keeps its signature and behaviour; only the web layer gains the step. Every host mounts the library's web manager, so every host gets the confirm; a host that calls `uninstall` programmatically keeps whatever gate it already has.
- screen: titled "Uninstall <name> <version>?" with `name` and `version` from the install record's manifest; then these lines: "removes the installed code of <domain>"; "removes the stored config of <domain>"; one line "clears retained topic <namespace> (tombstone)" for every `bus.publishes` entry of type STATE, or the single line "no retained topics to clear" when there is none; and "keeps the consent records and the install history". Hidden fields: the CSRF token, `sha256` (the install record's `manifest_sha256`) and `version`. Two submit buttons, `cancel` (value `cancel`) then `confirm uninstall` (value `confirm`), in that document order, so a bare Enter in the form cancels.
- state: a prepare from a state in which uninstall is refused (CXC-PC-LIFECYCLE-STATES) raises the existing transition refusal and renders no confirm screen.
- no-record: prepare and cancel write no consent record and no log event; a confirm writes the `uninstall` event through the manager (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-EVENT). Whether a cancelled uninstall should leave a consent record is ruled at CXC-PC-V02-RULING-UNINSTALL-RECORD: it does not.
- default: none.
- boundary-case: a POST without a valid CSRF token to either route is refused before any handler and changes nothing; with a denying auth hook both routes yield non-2xx and no handler body runs; `decision` repeated or unknown means cancel.
- verify-machine: through a WSGI client: `POST .../uninstall` and `POST .../uninstall/prepare` each return the confirm screen with `installs.json` and the install root byte-identical; `decide` with `cancel` redirects to the detail page and leaves both unchanged; `decide` with `confirm` uninstalls (the tombstone is published, the code and config are gone, the consent records remain, one `uninstall` event is appended); the detail page holds no form whose action ends in `/uninstall` and one whose action ends in `/uninstall/prepare`; the screen lists exactly the lines above for hello-world v1 (one STATE topic) and the "no retained topics" line for a plug-in with none; `cancel` precedes `confirm` in the document; the URL-prefix crawl of CXC-PC-UI-URL-PREFIX covers the new screen (every href, src, action and Location is relative or under the active SCRIPT_NAME); a missing CSRF token and a denying auth hook behave as stated.
- verify-human: on the glass an operator presses uninstall, reads what will be removed, presses cancel and sees the plug-in still installed, then repeats and confirms and sees it gone with its consent records still listed.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V02-T-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM-FLOW]
- evidence: PASS at composeio main e5c82fb000b8be82e0f14e4f4820da40736ea954 (PR #17, tag plugin-contract-v0.2, compose-plugins 0.2.0): python/compose_plugins/tests/test_v02_uninstall_confirm.py: test_CXC_PC_V02_T_UNINSTALL_CONFIRM_FLOW, test_CXC_PC_V02_T_UNINSTALL_CONFIRM_FLOW_csrf_and_auth, test_CXC_PC_V02_T_UNINSTALL_CONFIRM_FLOW_prepare_from_a_refused_state; the compose_plugins full suite at that commit: 1359 passed, 0 skipped, rc 0 (raw output sha256 d1fc46f1ce473da0f30ddab1894dd8a39ce5e3f32fd5a68025beec1eaaf52996; it counts these tests and does not list them by name); independent candidate review at that commit, round 2: PASS_WITH_NOTES. Filled 2026-11-27 from the build, review and push reports.
- evidence-fills-with: raw WSGI test output, the rendered confirm screen HTML, the library commit and the sha256 of each file
- decision-source: the web manager's uninstall has no confirm gate (spec 95 r24 CXC-PC-WEB-UI route set); taken as a library-level confirm for 0.2, as recorded in Gnomon spec 50 key slice-2-eula-answer-2026-11-27
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — ratified by DEC-SPEC95-V0-2-DELTA-RATIFIED-2026-11-27 (the confirm is decided as library-level; the routes, the screen and the no-record choice are the writer's)
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the library-level confirm is the contract owner's; the shape is the writer's
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-WEB-UI], [CXC-PC-UI-HOST-HOOKS], [CXC-PC-UI-URL-PREFIX], [CXC-PC-LIFECYCLE-UNINSTALL], [CXC-PC-V02-RULING-UNINSTALL-RECORD], [CXC-PC-V02-RULING-UNINSTALL-HOST-LINES]
- v0-3-delta: (0.3) The confirm screen gains the keep-or-delete choice for the plug-in's data folder, keep first and by default (CXC-PC-V03-UNINSTALL-DATA-CHOICE). The prepare and decide routes, the stale check and `cancel` are unchanged.

