### [CXC-PC-V03-LIFECYCLE-RECORD-COMPAT] A 0.3 reader reads both forms of `installs.jsonl`; a 0.2 reader reports 0.3 lines as malformed, and a roll-back can repeat `seq`

- consequence: Supersedes 0.2. CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-EVENT `not-events` lists a refused consent decision and `configure` as writing no event. From 0.3 both write an entry (`decline` and `configure`); a status change such as `parked` or `degraded`, and `PluginManager.record_decline`, still write none (CXC-PC-V03-RULING-RECORD-DECLINE-UNCHANGED).
- rule: Reader. a 0.3 reader accepts a line when it is a valid 0.2 event (eleven keys, plus the two abort keys on an `abort`) OR a valid 0.3 entry (those keys plus the three new keys, plus `data` on an `uninstall`); a line with only some of the three new keys, or an unknown key, is malformed under CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-MALFORMED-LINES (reason `bad-keys`), skipped and reported, never blocking.
- known-limit: a 0.2 library pointed at a state root where a 0.3 library wrote entries reports every 0.3 line as `malformed-line` with reason `bad-keys` (CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-MALFORMED-LINES): skipped for every purpose, never blocking. After a roll-back its new events take `seq` from the highest VALID line, so they can repeat the `seq` of skipped 0.3 lines. This is the same kind of limit as the 0.1 library meeting a 0.2 consent line that carries `eula_sha256` (CXC-PC-V02-STORES-COMPAT `known-limit`): hosts move their pin forward, and a roll-back after 0.3 entries exist needs a person.
- default: a state root written only by 0.2 or only by 0.3 reads without a finding.
- boundary-case: a line with only some of the three new keys, or with `data` on an event other than `uninstall`, is `bad-keys`.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2 check (e) of CXC-PC-V03-STORES-COMPAT: the 0.2 reader's `install_log_findings()` returns a `bad-keys` finding for each 0.3 line and nothing blocks; a 0.3 reader reads a mixed file of 0.2 and 0.3 lines with no finding.
- verify-human: none required.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw test output with the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the writer's; the limit is the cost of reusing the 0.2 log, ratified at CXC-PC-V03-RULING-LOG-KEYS
- basis: contract-owner design call
