### [CXC-PC-V03-WARNINGS] `warnings` is an optional list of `{id, title, text}` that the plug-in declares; each is shown on the consent page and needs its own acknowledgement

- rule: (1) `warnings` is an optional manifest field, valid only in a manifest that states `contract: "0.3"`. (2) Its value is a list of at most 8 objects whose ONLY keys are `id`, `title` and `text`; an unknown or missing key is refused naming it (the reading of CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS `validator-readings` (2)). (3) `id` matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}$` and is unique within the list. (4) `title` is non-empty and one line (`validator-readings` (12)), at most 120 code points. (5) `text` is non-empty under the blank rule of `validator-readings` (12), at most 2000 code points, and holds no control character other than line feed. (6) The consent content shows each warning with its title and its text verbatim (HTML-escaped on the web page, nothing else done to it), after the EULA block, in declared order, labelled "declared by the plug-in; not verified" (CXC-PC-V03-WARNING-ACK). (7) A warning is not a grant and is never enforced.
- default: absent means none declared.
- boundary-case: each is REFUSED at install naming the field or entry: a value that is not a list; an entry that is not an object; a missing or unknown key; an `id` that breaks the grammar or repeats; a blank, multi-line or over-long `title`; a blank, over-long or control-character `text`; more than 8 entries; the field in a manifest stating "0.1" or "0.2". ACCEPTED: `[]` and a single entry whose text spans three lines.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-CAPABILITIES-WARNINGS-TABLE.
- verify-human: an operator reads a consent screen with one declared warning and sees it on the same page as the EULA.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-CAPABILITIES-WARNINGS-TABLE]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw output of the table-driven test and the rendered consent page, with the library commit and the sha256 of each file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the field and its three keys are the contract owner's direction of 2026-11-28; the grammar, the bounds and the placement are the writer's
- basis: owner-decided (project owner)
