- procedure: one manifest per boundary case of CXC-PC-V03-CAPABILITIES and CXC-PC-V03-WARNINGS, each stating "0.3" except the version rows; the accepted examples; and a render of the consent content (`ConsentContent.text()` and the web page) for hello-world v1 stating "0.3" with `capabilities: ["agent-messaging"]` and two warnings.
- asserts: each refusal names exactly the field or entry; each accepted example installs; the render holds the capabilities line, then the EULA block when present, then the two warnings in declared order, each with its title and verbatim text; a manifest with neither field renders byte-identically to 0.2 apart from the page footer's contract version; the render makes no network call and no import of the plug-in module.
