### [CXC-PC-V03-UNINSTALL-DATA-CHOICE] The uninstall confirm offers keep (the default) or delete for the plug-in's data folder, the choice is recorded, and delete removes only that exact path inside the host state root

- rule: (1) The plug-in's data folder is the directory `Host.data_dir(domain)`; the base class returns `<state_root>/data/<domain>` (CXC-PC-V03-RULING-DATA-FOLDER). The library creates, reads and writes nothing in it; it only removes it, and only here. (2) `PluginManager.uninstall` gains the keyword-only optional `delete_data: bool = False` and `operator` (CXC-PC-V03-LIFECYCLE-RECORD-WRITE). (3) The web confirm screen (CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM) gains a choice named `data` with values `keep`, listed first and set by default, and `delete`, and a line naming the folder relative to the state root; `confirm` deletes only when the single `data` value is exactly `delete`, and any other value (missing, repeated, unknown) means keep. (4) A preflight runs BEFORE the log entry and before any side effect: when the folder does not exist the choice is `none`; otherwise `delete` is REFUSED, the whole uninstall with it and nothing changed, when the path is a symlink, when any component of it below the state root is a symlink, when its real path is not strictly inside the real state root, when it is not a directory, or when it is, or contains, the install root, the config store, `installs.json`, `installs.jsonl` or `consent.jsonl`. The refusal names the data folder and the reason. (5) Deletion removes the folder with `shutil.rmtree`; a symlink found inside it is removed as a link and never followed. (6) The uninstall entry's `data` key is `kept`, `deleted` or `none`; `deleted` is written ahead like the rest of the entry, and a failure leaves an `abort` entry.
- code-read: python/compose_plugins/compose_plugins/lifecycle.py `uninstall` (line 730) removes the install target with `shutil.rmtree(target)` (line 747) and the config with `self.configs.remove(domain)` (line 750); nothing in lifecycle.py, store.py or host.py names a plug-in data folder (`grep -i "data_dir"` in python/compose_plugins/compose_plugins finds none), so this node DEFINES it. host.py line 83 sets `self.install_root = self.state_root / "installed"`.
- default: keep.
- boundary-case: `delete` on a folder that is a symlink to a directory outside the state root is refused and the target is untouched; `delete` with no folder records `none`; a confirm that is stale under CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM-BINDING is refused before the data choice is read.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-UNINSTALL-DATA.
- verify-human: on the glass an operator uninstalls with the default and finds the data folder still there; uninstalls another with delete and finds it gone, and the log entry says which.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-UNINSTALL-DATA]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw output of the data-choice test and the two log lines, with the library commit and the sha256 of each file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — keep as the default, delete as the choice, the record of the choice and the refusal of a symlink or outside path are the contract owner's direction of 2026-11-28; the folder's definition and the preflight list are the writer's
- basis: owner-decided (project owner)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-LIFECYCLE-UNINSTALL], [CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM], [CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM-BINDING], [CXC-PC-V02-RULING-UNINSTALL-HOST-LINES], [CXC-PC-V03-LIFECYCLE-RECORD], [CXC-PC-V03-RULING-DATA-FOLDER]

