### [CXC-PC-V03-MOUNTABLE-WEB-MANAGER] The web manager honours the WSGI `SCRIPT_NAME`, so a host mounts it under a prefix unchanged

- rule: (1) A host mounts the app returned by `make_app(manager)` under any `SCRIPT_NAME` (Gnomon: `/plugin-manager`) with no wrapper, no rewriting and no host-specific code in the library. (2) Every link, form action and redirect starts with the active `SCRIPT_NAME`, a trailing `/` of which is ignored; routes are read from `PATH_INFO` only. (3) The CSRF defence, the auth hook and `extra_panels` behave identically under every prefix, and the pages added in 0.3 (the no-gate upgrade screen, the warning controls, the uninstall data choice) obey rule (2). (4) A gap found in mounting is fixed in the library (CXC-PC-V03-BASIS `fix-upstream`).
- note: Relation. this restates CXC-PC-UI-URL-PREFIX as a tested requirement of 0.3 and adds `/plugin-manager` to its mount list; the rule itself is unchanged.
- code-read: python/compose_plugins/compose_plugins/web.py line 108 `prefix = environ.get("SCRIPT_NAME", "").rstrip("/")`, line 137 `parts = [p for p in environ.get("PATH_INFO", "/").split("/") if p]`, and line 215 `raise _Response("303 See Other", "", [("Location", f"{prefix}{path}")])` already build every URL from `prefix` and read routes from `PATH_INFO`.
- default: an empty `SCRIPT_NAME` works.
- boundary-case: `SCRIPT_NAME` of `/plugin-manager/` (trailing slash) behaves as `/plugin-manager`; a request with `PATH_INFO` empty serves the index.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-MOUNT.
- verify-human: on Gnomon an operator opens the manager at `/plugin-manager` and follows every link without leaving the prefix.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-MOUNT]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw crawl output for each prefix, with the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — mounting under a host prefix unchanged is the contract owner's direction of 2026-11-28; the test list is the writer's
- basis: owner-decided (project owner)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-UI-URL-PREFIX], [CXC-PC-WEB-UI], [CXC-PC-UI-HOST-HOOKS], [CXC-PC-V03-BASIS]

