### [CXC-PC-V03-HOST-AGENT-BLOCK] A host that mounts the web manager MUST keep every state-changing route out of agents' reach; read-only routes MAY be reachable

- rule: (1) A host that mounts the web manager MUST keep every state-changing route under its mount out of agents' reach: install and upgrade prepare and decide, consent, warning acknowledgement, enable, disable, configure, uninstall and its confirm. (2) Read-only routes (index, detail, status) MAY be reachable by agents. (3) The host chooses the means, for example a prefix block at its router. (4) The library cannot tell a person from an agent, so this is a host obligation, not a library check; the library adds no agent test and its auth hook and CSRF defence are unchanged.
- why: with the consent click in the browser as the operator's only consent, an agent that can reach a state-changing route can answer consent for the operator; the guide's rule that an agent never does so (CXC-PA-NO-CONSENT-BY-AGENT) needs a wall behind it.
- code-read: python/compose_plugins/compose_plugins/web.py lines 154 to 193 route every state-changing action (`install/prepare`, `install/decide`, `plugin/<domain>/enable`, `disable`, `uninstall/prepare`, `uninstall/decide`, `configure`, `upgrade/prepare`, `upgrade/decide`) through POST, and lines 145 to 153 and 194 to 195 serve the read-only index, consent records, panels and detail page by GET; line 110 `identity = self.host.auth_hook(environ)` is the only identity the library sees.
- default: none; a host that does not mount the web manager has no such routes.
- boundary-case: a prepare route changes nothing but is still blocked, because it renders the consent page the decide route answers; the consent-records page and `extra_panels` pages are read-only and may be reachable.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-HOST-AGENT-BLOCK.
- verify-human: on the host, an operator confirms that a request attributed to an agent cannot reach any state-changing route and can still open the index.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-HOST-AGENT-BLOCK]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw output of the route table test run against each host, with the host commit and the sha256 of the output file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis
- basis: contract-owner design call
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-UI-HOST-HOOKS], [CXC-PC-RULE-CONSENT-HOST-OWNED], [CXC-PC-CONSENT-GATES], [CXC-PC-V03-MOUNTABLE-WEB-MANAGER], [CXC-PC-V03-CONSENT-TRIGGERS], [CXC-PC-V02-UNINSTALL-CONFIRM]

### [CXC-PC-V03-T-HOST-AGENT-BLOCK] Test: an agent-attributed request to each state-changing route is refused by the host before the library, and the read-only routes still answer

- procedure: mount the web manager behind the host's real router and agent block; send, as an identity the host classes as an agent, one request to each state-changing route (`install/prepare`, `install/decide`, `plugin/<domain>/enable`, `disable`, `configure`, `upgrade/prepare`, `upgrade/decide`, `uninstall`, `uninstall/prepare`, `uninstall/decide`) with a valid CSRF token and a spy behind the mount; then one GET to the index, a detail page and the consent-records page.
- asserts: every state-changing request is refused by the host (a non-2xx answer) and the spy behind the mount, the consent gate, the log and `installs.json` record zero calls and no change; each read-only GET answers 200; the same requests as an operator identity reach the library.
- verify-machine: non-zero exit on any state-changing route that reaches the library or any read-only route that does not answer.
- verify-human: none required.
- evidence: EMPTY
- status: proposed
