### [CXC-PC-V03-MANIFEST-FROZEN] The manifest schema is FROZEN at 0.3: a field is added only by a new contract version under the additive rule, and no field is removed or retyped

- rule: (1) From ratification, 2026-11-28, the set of manifest fields below is the frozen set; the freeze is in force as of that date, before any build and before the tag. (2) A later contract adds a field only as a new MINOR under CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE (2): the new field is optional, valid only in a manifest that states that contract or a later one, and no existing field becomes required. (3) No later contract removes a field, renames it, retypes it, narrows what it accepts, or changes what a value means; a manifest valid under 0.3 stays valid, with the same meaning, under every later MINOR of the same MAJOR (a change of meaning is a MAJOR, CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE (3)). (4) The frozen artifact is `manifest-0.3.schema.json`, generated from the validator's patterns (CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS `validator-readings` (15)); it never changes after the tag. (5) A reader or an agent cites THIS node for the field set. (6) Two open questions were closed so that they only add: undefined well-formed capability tokens are accepted forever (CXC-PC-V03-RULING-UNKNOWN-CAPABILITY-TOKENS), and the grant-bearing lists drive advisories only, so changing them never narrows acceptance (CXC-PC-V03-RULING-GRANT-TOKENS).
- claim: Frozen fields. the table below lists every field at 0.3: name, requiredness, JSON type, and the first contract that defines it.

| field | requiredness at 0.3 | JSON type | defined from |
|---|---|---|---|
| `contract` | required | string `"MAJOR.MINOR"`: "0.1", "0.2" or "0.3" | 0.1 |
| `domain` | required | string | 0.1 |
| `name` | required | string | 0.1 |
| `version` | required | string, SemVer | 0.1 |
| `description` | required | string | 0.1 |
| `documentation` | required | string, https URL | 0.1 |
| `requirements` | required (may be `[]`) | list of strings | 0.1 |
| `run` | required | object `{form, entry}` | 0.1 |
| `hosts` | required | object, at least one key | 0.1 |
| `issue_tracker` | optional | string, URL | 0.1 |
| `codeowners` | optional | list of strings | 0.1 |
| `isolation_floor` | optional | string, `inprocess` or `subprocess` | 0.1 |
| `bus` | optional | object `{publishes, subscribes}` | 0.1 |
| `standard_questions` | optional | string, relative directory path | 0.1 |
| `permissions` | optional | object `{network, filesystem}` | 0.1 |
| `license` | optional | string, SPDX expression | 0.2 |
| `eula` | optional | string, package-relative file path | 0.2 |
| `capabilities` | optional | list of strings | 0.3 |
| `warnings` | optional | list of objects `{id, title, text}` | 0.3 |
| `config_schema` | generated; always present in a built manifest | object, a JSON Schema | 0.1 |

- default: none.
- boundary-case: a proposal that adds a field to 0.3 itself after ratification is a new contract version, not an edit; a proposal that makes `capabilities` required, or removes `standard_questions`, is refused by this node.
- verify-machine: a pinning test holds the 0.3 field names, their requiredness and JSON types as a literal, and fails when the validator or the shipped schema drops, renames, retypes or newly requires any of them; the shipped 0.3 schema equals the generated one (the existing drift check); CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2.
- verify-human: none required — structural.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw output of the pinning test with the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the freeze and its additive rule are the contract owner's direction of 2026-11-28; the field table, the monotone-acceptance wording and the pinning test are the writer's
- basis: owner-decided (project owner)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-MANIFEST-FIELDS], [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS], [CXC-PC-RESERVED-NAMES], [CXC-PC-V03-VERSION-0-3], [CXC-PC-V03-READS-0-2-UNCHANGED]

### [CXC-PC-V03-READS-0-2-UNCHANGED] A 0.3 library reads contract "0.2" and "0.1" manifests unchanged, and the 0.2 conformance fixtures stay in the suite unmodified

- rule: (1) For a manifest that states "0.1" or "0.2", a 0.3 library validates, renders, hashes and installs exactly as a 0.2 library: the same refusals naming the same fields, the same `granted` set, the same `manifest_sha256`. (2) The conformance fixtures `hello_world_v1`, `hello_world_v2` and `hello_world_eula`, and their plug-in code, stay in the suite UNMODIFIED, byte for byte (digests below); a 0.3 fixture is a new directory, never an edit of these. (3) The consent content of each is byte-identical to 0.2's apart from the page footer's contract version, the one exception CXC-PC-V02-STORES-COMPAT `page-identity` already states. (4) The conformance script runs the nine steps and NC1 to NC8 against these fixtures, then NC9 and NC10 (CXC-PC-V03-NC-UPGRADE-DECLINED, CXC-PC-V03-NC-GRANT-BEARING-CONFIG), with NC3's input moved to "0.4" (CXC-PC-V03-VERSION-0-3 `negative-control-input`).
- note: Fixture digests. sha256 of each file at composeio main 0c6bb2886b711fe78b0cc0e2f56a5d5c6c2c6ce8 under python/compose_plugins/compose_plugins/fixtures/: hello_world_v1/manifest.json d877dec1a9863eca1007b81cb363841e6932fdd435437972106038e584d49b21; hello_world_v1/hello_world/plugin.py f720ffa6f4526cd214e4fcdb05ed07b25fe1b16b33a47aae28b6fd3fa986d0df; hello_world_v2/manifest.json f57b34efb08ec25e0bd2530add1892045e2ae01f28207fa326ddda8e0dad5fe0; hello_world_v2/hello_world/plugin.py d9b67cedbf6e7ab75823a4eb31a2d8cc8d4d3cca9dcd242ab671af743677cdea; hello_world_eula/manifest.json 18dbd0d33e92154f0482886bed5b61af462da61b8f0fde9f161ab337a7e1f56d; hello_world_eula/EULA.txt 9bc1644fa4fe198412e0ef70f44646b00dd13ca5238b2fbf82b3c8494c34bf0b; hello_world_eula/hello_world/plugin.py f720ffa6f4526cd214e4fcdb05ed07b25fe1b16b33a47aae28b6fd3fa986d0df.
- default: none.
- boundary-case: a 0.2 manifest whose `config_schema` has a property named `path` installs on a 0.3 host (CXC-PC-V03-VERSION-0-3 rule (4)).
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2.
- verify-human: none required.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw output of the compatibility test and of the 0.2 test files run unmodified against the 0.3 library, with the library commit and the sha256 of each output
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the compatibility rule is the contract owner's direction of 2026-11-28; the digests and the page-identity carry-over are the writer's
- basis: contract-owner design call
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-V02-STORES-COMPAT], [CXC-PC-V02-VERSION-0-2], [CXC-PC-HELLO-V1], [CXC-PC-HELLO-V2], [CXC-PC-CONFORMANCE-SCRIPT], [CXC-PC-V03-MANIFEST-FROZEN]

### [CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2] Test: the 0.2 fixtures are unmodified, every 0.2 test still passes against the 0.3 library, and the field set is pinned

- procedure: hash every fixture file listed at CXC-PC-V03-READS-0-2-UNCHANGED; run the 0.2 test files (test_v02_*.py and the earlier suites) unmodified against the 0.3 library; run the conformance script at both isolation levels; run the field-set pinning test of CXC-PC-V03-MANIFEST-FROZEN.
- asserts: each digest equals the listed value; every 0.2 test passes except those whose assertion is the library's own contract constant or the sole NC3 input, each such exception named in the output; the script passes steps 1 to 9 and NC1 to NC10; the pinning test passes.
- verify-machine: non-zero exit on any mismatch.
- verify-human: none required.
- evidence: EMPTY
- status: proposed
- basis: contract-owner design call
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-V03-READS-0-2-UNCHANGED], [CXC-PC-V03-MANIFEST-FROZEN]

### [CXC-PC-V03-STORES-COMPAT] The state files change additively for hosts; a 0.2 library that reads a 0.3 consent line or log line reports or refuses it loudly instead of misreading it

- host-protocol: `Host` gains two OPTIONAL members, `policy` (CXC-PC-V03-HOST-POLICY-HOOK) and `data_dir` (CXC-PC-V03-UNINSTALL-DATA-CHOICE), each with a base-class default. A `Host` written against 0.2 constructs and runs under 0.3 unchanged.
- manager-signatures: only new optional keyword arguments and new exceptions: `operator` on `configure`, `enable`, `disable`, `uninstall`; `delete_data` on `uninstall`; `acknowledged_warnings` on `install` and `upgrade`; `OperatorDeclined`, `PolicyRefused`, `WarningAckRefused`. No 0.2 signature loses or reorders a parameter.
- installs-json: the top level stays `{domain: record}`. A record gains two optional keys, `capabilities` and `warning_digests` (CXC-PC-V03-DECLARATION-CHANGE-PREDICATE), omitted when empty; a 0.2 record has neither and reads as empty. A 0.3 library reads a 0.2 file unchanged.
- consent-jsonl: a record gains ONE more optional key, `acknowledged_warnings` (CXC-PC-V03-WARNING-ACK); the reader accepts the eight keys plus `eula_sha256` and `acknowledged_warnings` when each is valid, and refuses any other key set naming the key. A record for a manifest without warnings is byte-identical in shape to 0.2's.
- installs-jsonl: entries gain `operator`, `result`, `consent_id` and, on an `uninstall`, `data`; the event names `configure` and `decline` are new (CXC-PC-V03-LIFECYCLE-RECORD). A 0.3 reader reads 0.2 lines unchanged.
- known-limit: a 0.2 library pointed at a state root where a 0.3 library wrote entries reports every 0.3 `installs.jsonl` line as `malformed-line` with reason `bad-keys` (skipped for every purpose, never blocking), so a roll-back appends new events with `seq` values that may repeat those of the skipped 0.3 lines; and it refuses loudly a consent line that carries `acknowledged_warnings` ("keys must be exactly ..."). Hosts move their pin forward; a roll-back after warnings were acknowledged needs a person.
- verify-machine: CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2 covers (a) a state root written by the 0.2 library loads under 0.3 and its first 0.3 entry takes the next `seq`; (b) a 0.2-style stub `Host` drives steps 1 to 9; (c) a consent line with an unknown key is refused naming it; (d) a consent line with a non-hex digest in `acknowledged_warnings` is refused naming it; (e) a 0.3 log line is reported by the 0.2 reader as `bad-keys` and nothing blocks.
- verify-human: none required.
- tested-by: [CXC-PC-V03-T-READS-0-2]
- evidence: EMPTY
- evidence-fills-with: the raw test output with the library commit and the sha256 of the output file
- status: ratified
- status-detail: ratified 2026-11-28 by composeux-architect, contract owner
- provenance: architect-synthesis — the writer's, following the shape of CXC-PC-V02-STORES-COMPAT
- basis: contract-owner design call
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-PLUGIN-CONTRACT]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-V02-STORES-COMPAT], [CXC-PC-CONSENT-RECORD], [CXC-PC-V02-INSTALL-LOG-MALFORMED-LINES], [CXC-PC-V03-LIFECYCLE-RECORD], [CXC-PC-V03-WARNING-ACK], [CXC-PC-V03-HOST-POLICY-HOOK], [CXC-PC-V03-UNINSTALL-DATA-CHOICE]

